# dashboard service identity (canonical, fixed): user and group dashboard,
# UID/GID 178. The dashboard binds the unprivileged port 8899 and only
# reads the world-readable queue database, so it runs from first start
# as its own identity and needs no root phase, no supplementary groups,
# and no state of its own (home is /var/lib/dashboard, created for a
# process that writes nothing).
# UID 178 is the first free ID above 177 plugdev: accounts.tsv carries
# no 178-199 and no tree fragment claims one (the tree-wide "178" hits
# are kernel enum values and patch line numbers, not identities) -
# verified before assigning; never reuse it for another identity.
user dashboard 178 dashboard /var/lib/dashboard /sbin/nologin
group dashboard 178
dir /var/lib/dashboard 0755 dashboard dashboard
